# Environment variables (never commit real values)

Copy to `.env.local` for local development. These files are gitignored.

```bash
cp .env.example .env.local
```

## OpenAI (productivity PDF import, sales note scan, DMS parsing)

| Variable | Local | Netlify production |
|----------|-------|-------------------|
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | `.env.local` | Site settings → Environment variables → **Functions** scope |

Run locally with `npm run dev` (Express reads `.env.local`). After changing Netlify variables, **redeploy**.

**Never** put API keys in source code, GitHub, or client-side env vars (`VITE_*`). Keys stay server-side only.

## Firebase (client — safe to expose in frontend)

Use `VITE_FIREBASE_*` in `.env.local` for local builds. Set the same names in Netlify **Build** scope if needed.

## Optional

- `GEMINI_API_KEY` — server-only Gemini routes
- `SYSTEM_WORKERS_PASSWORD` — internal worker auth
